        "original_id": "86d1ec87-e0d4-52c8-8983-2291f6f3464d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Turner Field, Centennial Olympic Stadium, Atlanta\n- Organizations: Atlanta Braves\n- Events: 1996 Summer Olympics, 1996 Summer Paralympics, 2013 Atlanta Braves season\n\nFacts:\n- In 1996, Centennial Olympic Stadium was built as the centerpiece of the 1996 Summer Olympics in Atlanta.\n- In 1996, Centennial Olympic Stadium was the 85,000-seat main stadium of the 1996 Summer Olympic Games and the 1996 Summer Paralympic Games in Atlanta.\n- After the 1996 Summer Olympics, Centennial Olympic Stadium was converted into a baseball park that became the new home of the Atlanta Braves as Turner Field.\n- In 2013, the Atlanta Braves played their 17th season of home games at Turner Field.\n- In 2013, the Atlanta Braves were in their 48th season in Atlanta and their 143rd season overall.",
